 service, or a local process such as Winlogon.exe or Services.exe.\r\r\n\r\r\nThe logon type field indicates the kind of logon that occurred. The most common types are 2 (interactive) and 3 (network).\r\r\n\r\r\nThe New Logon fields indicate the account for whom the new logon was created, i.e. the account that was logged on.\r\r\n\r\r\nThis event is generated when the Audit Group Membership subcategory is configured.  The Logon ID field can be used to correlate this event with the corresponding user logon event as well as to any other security audit events generated during this logon session.\r\nevt-00018|4634|2026-05-06T00:00:00.007Z|||An account was logged off.\r\r\n\r\r\nSubject:\r\r\n\tSecurity ID:\t\tS-1-5-18\r\r\n\tAccount Name:\t\tDC01$\r\r\n\tAccount Domain:\t\tCORP\r\r\n\tLogon ID:\t\t0x51C3B8\r\r\n\r\r\nLogon Type:\t\t\t3\r\r\n\r\r\nThis event is generated when a logon session is destroyed. It may be positively correlated with a logon event using the Logon ID value. Logon IDs are only unique between reboots on the same computer.\r\nevt-00019|3|2026-05-06T00:00:02.000Z|C:\\Windows\\ADWS\\Microsoft.ActiveDirectory.WebServices.exe||Network connection detected:\r\r\nRuleName: -\r\r\nUtcTime: 2020-09-04 20:09:39.150\r\r\nProcessGuid: {ee23f965-8a44-5f52-4d00-000000000400}\r\r\nProcessId: 3312\r\r\nImage: C:\\Windows\\ADWS\\Microsoft.ActiveDirectory.WebServices.exe\r\r\nUser: NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM\r\r\nProtocol: tcp\r\r\nInitiated: true\r\r\nSourceIsIpv6: true\r\r\nSourceIp: 0:0:0:0:0:0:0:1\r\r\nSourceHostname: -\r\r\nSourcePort: 63704\r\r\nSourcePortName: -\r\r\nDestinationIsIpv6: true\r\r\nDestinationIp: 0:0:0:0:0:0:0:1\r\r\nDestinationHostname: -\r\r\nDestinationPort: 389\r\r\nDestinationPortName: -\r\nevt-00020|3|2026-05-06T00:00:02.001Z|C:\\Windows\\System32\\lsass.exe||Network connection detected:\r\r\nRuleName: -\r\r\nUtcTime: 2020-09-04 20:09:39.150\r\r\nProcessGuid: {ee23f965-8a2d-5f52-0c00-000000000400}\r\r\nProcessId: 700\r\r\nImage: C:\\Windows\\Syste